window.DI_SEARCH_INDEX = [{"k":"page","t":"Code map: the folder tree","u":"code/index.html","s":"Every folder of the DeepInfer repository at commit 9bd9cf2, with file and line counts, a short description, and links to the module and concept pages.","sec":"Code map","lvl":"","h":["Purpose","The folder tree","How the folders depend on each other","How the numbers were measured","Related pages"]},{"k":"page","t":"engine/llm_engine.py: the LLMEngine class","u":"code/llm-engine.html","s":"LLMEngine starts the workers, sizes the KV cache, owns the C++ scheduler, and runs one engine step each time LLM calls step().","sec":"Code map","lvl":"Intermediate","h":["Purpose","Where it sits","Who calls it","What it calls","Key classes and functions","Walk through the main methods","Start-up: __init__","_init_workers: processes for context parallelism","_init_cache: how many KV blocks","add_request: from token ids to a sequence","step: one engine step","post_process and _process_model_outputs","pre_sampler_sync and DeferredRelease","The small methods","Deep dive","Data flow of one step: objects, shapes and types","Processes and threads around the engine","How the engine works with zero-overhead scheduling (ZOS)","Sizing the KV cache: the numbers","Error paths: what raises, what only logs","Environment variables that this file reads","Hook methods for parts that are not in this release","Related concepts","Check yourself","Related pages"]},{"k":"page","t":"Hardware platforms: NVIDIA and Ascend","u":"concepts/hardware-platforms.html","s":"DeepInfer runs on NVIDIA GPUs and on Huawei Ascend NPUs. At start-up it makes one Platform object, and the shared code reads all hardware choices from it.","sec":"DeepInfer concepts","lvl":"Intermediate","h":["The idea","The picture","In the code","Step 1: detect the hardware without PyTorch","Step 2: make the Platform object, once","Step 3: the two classes","Step 4: shared code uses the platform","Step 5: Ascend-only patches","Step 6: build time","Deep dive","accelerator_kind(): the exact detection rules","PlatformNPU.__init__, line by line","Pinned host memory on both platforms","Communication: backends, options and SM limits","The kernel dispatcher ops.py, line by line","fp8_sf_type: why int32 on NVIDIA and int16 on Ascend","The npu_ops import hook in detail","Two builds in one source tree: deepinfer/_so/<accelerator>-<arch>","Build time: extension sources, vendor libraries, requirements","Is DeepInfer AFD (Attention-FFN Disaggregation)?","What can go wrong","Check yourself","Related pages"]},{"k":"page","t":"DeepInfer Explained","u":"index.html","s":"A study guide to the DeepInfer inference engine for Python developers who know little about machine learning. It starts simple and goes down to the exact code.","sec":"Home","lvl":"","h":["The system map","Start here","A. New to machine learning","B. You know how LLMs work","C. You study one part","How to use this site","What is not in this release","The code version this site explains"]},{"k":"page","t":"The KV cache","u":"learn/kv-cache.html","s":"The KV cache keeps the keys and values of earlier tokens, so each new token needs only its own keys and values. DeepInfer stores the cache in blocks of 128 tokens.","sec":"Learn the basics","lvl":"Beginner","h":["The idea","Why keep keys and values?","A worked example","An everyday comparison","How much memory does it use?","Blocks and block tables","When the blocks run out: preemption","The picture","Try it: a block allocator","In the code","Step 1: one block holds 128 tokens","Step 2: the BlockManager hands out blocks","Step 3: the cache has several parts","Step 4: the cache size comes from a memory profile","Deep dive","Memory per token: the formulas with DeepInfer numbers","From token position to byte: the slot mapping","The BlockManager, line by line","Preemption in DeepInfer, step by step","Where the memory comes from: the profile run","What can go wrong","Check yourself","Related pages"]},{"k":"page","t":"Environment variables","u":"reference/env-vars.html","s":"DeepInfer reads 59 DEEPINFER_* environment variables through one class, envs, in deepinfer/environ.py. This page lists each variable with its type, default, effect and the code that reads it, and tells when the value is read.","sec":"Reference","lvl":"Intermediate","h":["What an environment variable is","How DeepInfer reads a variable","The EnvVar descriptor","How the text becomes a value","When DeepInfer reads a variable","Set variables before you import deepinfer","Variables read at import time","Values that the code changes at run time","All DEEPINFER variables","Platform (1)","Runtime (2)","Distributed Communication (4)","MoE & Expert Parallelism (8)","Attention (2)","MTP (4)","Model Loading (2)","Sampling (2)","CUDA Graph (6)","KV Cache Store (3)","Structured Output (5)","Scheduling (3)","Logging (4)","YoCo (2)","Profiling & Debug (7)","Multi-Modal (4)","Other DEEPINFER names outside environ.py","Other environment variables that DeepInfer sets or needs","Read by DeepInfer","Set by DeepInfer","Common recipes","Choose the platform build","Run the examples from a local model copy","DSpark: confidence-scheduled verification","Decoder SWA bounded replay (YOCO)","Asynchronous scheduling","Batch-invariant inference","Deterministic sampling","Deep dive","One variable end to end: DEEPINFER_USE_NEXTN_DECODE","EnvVar.__get__ in detail: lock, cache check and errors","Derived variables: values that read other variables","Docstrings in environ.py, translated","Prefill vote points with real numbers (70 and 100)","CUDA graph batch sizes with real numbers","EPLB variables together, with real numbers","Automatic SM count for DeepEP (DEEPINFER_USERBUFFER_COMM_SMS=0)","What can go wrong","Check yourself","Related pages"]},{"k":"page","t":"Tour: Life of a request","u":"tours/life-of-a-request.html","s":"Follow one request from llm.generate() to its output tokens in 13 stops: tokenizer, admission, C++ scheduler, batch metadata, worker step, forward pass, KV cache, sampler, draft tokens and output objects.","sec":"Guided tours","lvl":"Beginner","h":["The idea","The picture","Processes and threads","1The user script starts the engine and calls generate()","Stop 1 in detail: processes, devices and settings","2The public API: LLM.generate() and _add_request()","Stop 2 in detail: defaults that LLM sets","3Tokenization: text becomes token ids","Stop 3 in detail: tokenizer class, vision models and Engram","4Admission: LLMEngine.add_request() makes a C++ Sequence","Stop 4 in detail: the Sequence object, schedulable, and the helpers","5Scheduling in C++: which requests run in this step","Stop 5 in detail: limits, blocks, decode steps and preemption","6Batch metadata: from sequences to tensors","Stop 6 in detail: the tensors of a prefill step and a decode step","7The worker step: forward N, post-process N-1, sample N","Stop 7 in detail: why the CPU is one step behind, and how the device catches up","8The forward pass: the model runs on the device","Stop 8 in detail: what this tour does not open","9The KV cache: what this step writes","Stop 9 in detail: sizes, slots and what a decode step writes","10Sampling: the sampler selects the next token","Stop 10 in detail: inputs, force-top-k, and results on the CPU","11Draft tokens: DFlash guesses the next tokens","Stop 11 in detail: placeholder drafts, confidence and DSpark","12Output assembly: the engine updates the sequence and builds outputs","Stop 12 in detail: process_outputs line by line, and the output pool","13Back to the user: tokens and text","Stop 13 in detail: has_unfinished_requests and the end of the loop","The loop: many steps for one request","What can go wrong","Check yourself","Related pages"]},{"k":"page","t":"Glossary","u":"reference/glossary.html","s":"Short definitions of every technical term on this site, with links to the pages that explain them.","sec":"Reference","lvl":"","h":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I","K","L","M","N","P","Q","R","S","T","V","Z"]},{"k":"term","t":"accelerator","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-accelerator","s":"A chip that does AI math much faster than a CPU. In DeepInfer, an accelerator is an NVIDIA GPU or a Huawei Ascend NPU.","a":["device"]},{"k":"term","t":"AFD","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-afd","s":"Attention-FFN Disaggregation. A design that runs attention layers and FFN (expert) layers on different groups of devices. DeepInfer does not use it.","a":["Attention-FFN Disaggregation"]},{"k":"term","t":"attention","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-attention","s":"The layer step where each token looks at the earlier tokens. It compares its query with their keys and makes a weighted sum of their values.","a":["self-attention"]},{"k":"term","t":"attention head","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-attention-head","s":"One independent copy of attention inside a layer. A layer has several heads; each head has its own queries, keys and values of size head_dim.","a":["head","heads","head_dim","kv heads"]},{"k":"term","t":"BlockManager","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-block-manager","s":"The C++ object that owns the free list of KV cache blocks. It gives blocks to sequences and takes them back.","a":["block manager","state_manager"]},{"k":"term","t":"block table","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-block-table","s":"A list per sequence that maps its logical block 0, 1, 2 ... to physical block ids in the KV cache pool.","a":["block_table","page table"]},{"k":"term","t":"CANN","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-cann","s":"Compute Architecture for Neural Networks. Huawei's software stack (driver, runtime, libraries) for Ascend NPUs. It has the same role as CUDA.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"chunked prefill","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-chunked-prefill","s":"Splitting a long prompt into parts that run in several prefill steps, so that one step never has more than max_num_batched_tokens tokens.","a":["chunk","chunked_prefill"]},{"k":"term","t":"collective operation","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-collective","s":"A communication step in which all ranks of a group take part, for example all-reduce, all-gather or all-to-all.","a":["collective"]},{"k":"term","t":"context parallelism","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-context-parallelism","s":"Several devices share the tokens of one long prefill. In DeepInfer, CP ranks are extra worker processes that receive their inputs from the driver.","a":["CP","mirror CP"]},{"k":"term","t":"CUDA","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-cuda","s":"NVIDIA's programming model, compiler and runtime for its GPUs. PyTorch calls it through the torch.cuda module.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"CUDA graph","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-cuda-graph","s":"A recording of all kernel launches of one forward pass for a fixed batch size. A replay starts all kernels with one call, so the CPU cost is small.","a":["graph replay","cudagraph"]},{"k":"term","t":"data parallelism","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-data-parallelism","s":"DP. Several devices run the same model part, and each device works on different requests.","a":["DP"]},{"k":"term","t":"decode","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-decode","s":"The second phase of generation. Each step makes one new token per sequence (more with speculative decoding) and adds its keys and values to the KV cache.","a":["decode step","decoding"]},{"k":"term","t":"DeepEP","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-deepep","s":"DeepSeek's communication library for MoE. Its dispatch step sends tokens to the devices of their experts. Its combine step brings the results back.","a":["dispatch","combine"]},{"k":"term","t":"descriptor","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-descriptor","s":"A Python object that is stored as a class attribute and controls what an attribute read returns, through its __get__ method.","a":["__get__","non-data descriptor","EnvVar"]},{"k":"term","t":"DFlash","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-dflash","s":"The draft module of DeepInfer. In each decode step, the sampler calls it once after the draft check, and it proposes the drafts for the next step.","a":["MTP_module","draft model"]},{"k":"term","t":"draft token","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-draft-token","s":"A guessed next token from the MTP module. The next decode step sends it as input, and the sampler accepts or rejects it.","a":["draft","drafts","nextn token"]},{"k":"term","t":"driver worker","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-driver-worker","s":"The Worker object that runs in the same process as LLMEngine. It does the model work for its rank and sends each method call to the other context-parallel ranks.","a":["driver_worker","follower worker"]},{"k":"term","t":"dtype","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-dtype","s":"The number format of a tensor, for example bfloat16, float8 or int32. It sets how many bytes each value uses.","a":["data type"]},{"k":"term","t":"engine callbacks","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-engine-callbacks","s":"Two engine functions that the driver worker calls during a step: pre_sampler_sync after sampling starts, and post_process when a step's results are ready.","a":["EngineCallbacks","post_process","pre_sampler_sync"]},{"k":"term","t":"engine step","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-engine-step","s":"One call of LLMEngine.step(): schedule a batch, run the model once on the device, sample, and update the requests. Generation is a loop of steps.","a":["step","iteration"]},{"k":"term","t":"environment variable","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-environment-variable","s":"A named text value that a process gets when it starts, for example CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1. DeepInfer reads many settings this way.","a":["env var"]},{"k":"term","t":"EOS token","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-eos-token","s":"End of sequence: a special token that tells the engine to stop a request. In the release tokenizer, EOS has id 1 and BOS (begin of sequence) has id 0.","a":["EOS","BOS","end of sequence"]},{"k":"term","t":"E/P/D disaggregation","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-epd","s":"A deployment that runs the vision encoder (E), prefill (P) and decode (D) as separate model instances. It is not included in this DeepInfer release.","a":["EPD","VE/Prefill/Decode"]},{"k":"term","t":"expert parallelism","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-expert-parallelism","s":"EP. The experts of an MoE layer are split across devices. Tokens go to the devices that hold their experts, and the results come back.","a":["EP"]},{"k":"term","t":"extension module","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-extension-module","s":"A compiled library (a .so file) that Python imports like a normal module. deepinfer._C is DeepInfer's C++ extension module.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"FP8","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-fp8","s":"An 8-bit floating-point number format. It uses half the memory of BF16. It needs scale factors to keep enough precision.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"fragmentation","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-fragmentation","s":"Memory that is reserved but not used. With paging, only the last block of each sequence can be partly empty (internal fragmentation).","a":["internal fragmentation","external fragmentation","wasted slots"]},{"k":"term","t":"git submodule","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-git-submodule","s":"A folder in a git repository that points to a commit of another repository. A plain clone leaves the folder empty until you run git submodule update.","a":["submodule"]},{"k":"term","t":"Gloo","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-gloo","s":"A torch.distributed backend that sends CPU tensors over the network. DeepInfer uses it for CPU-side groups and for the first start-up connection.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"GPU","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-gpu","s":"Graphics Processing Unit. A chip with thousands of small cores that do the same operation on many values at the same time.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"HCCL","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-hccl","s":"Huawei Collective Communication Library. It moves tensors between Ascend NPUs. torch_npu adds it to PyTorch as the \"hccl\" backend.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"hidden state","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-hidden-state","s":"The vector that represents one token inside the model. The embedding makes it from the token id; each layer changes it.","a":["hidden states","hidden_states"]},{"k":"term","t":"import hook","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-import-hook","s":"Code that changes what a Python import statement returns. DeepInfer's npu_ops package uses one to replace two vendor functions on Ascend.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"import time","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-import-time","s":"The moment when Python runs the top level of a module for the first time: module code, class bodies and the default values of function arguments.","a":["at import","module level"]},{"k":"term","t":"kernel","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-kernel","s":"A small program that runs on the GPU or NPU. One kernel does one operation, for example a matrix multiply, on many values in parallel.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"kernel factory","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-kernel-factory","s":"In DeepInfer, a function named ..._tl. You call it with fixed parameters (sizes or dtypes), and it returns a compiled TileLang kernel that you then call with tensors.","a":["_tl factory"]},{"k":"term","t":"block","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-kv-block","s":"A fixed-size part of the KV cache that holds the keys and values of a fixed number of tokens. In DeepInfer one block holds 128 tokens for all layers.","a":["KV block","cache block","page","physical block"]},{"k":"term","t":"KV cache","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-kv-cache","s":"Device memory that keeps the keys and values of earlier tokens, so that each new token does not compute them again.","a":["key-value cache","kv-cache","kvcache"]},{"k":"term","t":"KV compression","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-kv-compression","s":"Storing one cache entry for every n tokens instead of one per token. DeepInfer supports the ratios 1 and 2 (C1, C2).","a":["compressed attention","compress ratio","kv_compress_ratio","C1","C2"]},{"k":"term","t":"LLM","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-llm","s":"Large language model. A neural network that reads tokens and predicts the next token, one token at a time.","a":["large language model","language model"]},{"k":"term","t":"LLMEngine","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-llm-engine","s":"The Python class that owns the scheduler, the KV block managers and the driver worker. LLM calls its step() again and again until all requests finish.","a":["engine","llm_engine"]},{"k":"term","t":"logits","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-logits","s":"One raw score per vocabulary token. Softmax turns the scores into probabilities. DeepInfer computes them in float32 only for the rows that it samples.","a":["logit"]},{"k":"term","t":"logprob","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-logprob","s":"The natural logarithm of the probability of a token. Each RequestOutput carries the logprob of its token and, on request, of the best alternatives.","a":["log probability","top_logprobs","token_logprobs"]},{"k":"term","t":"memory profiling","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-memory-profiling","s":"A test forward pass at start-up. It measures the peak device memory of the model, so that the engine knows how much memory is left for the KV cache.","a":["profile run","profile_run","profile_num_available_blocks"]},{"k":"term","t":"MoE","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-moe","s":"Mixture of Experts. A layer with many small feed-forward networks (experts). A router sends each token to only a few of them.","a":["Mixture of Experts"]},{"k":"term","t":"monkeypatch","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-monkeypatch","s":"A pytest fixture that changes an attribute, a dict item or an environment variable for one test, and puts the old value back after the test.","a":["monkeypatch.setattr","monkeypatch.setenv"]},{"k":"term","t":"MTP","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-mtp","s":"Multi-token prediction: a module that predicts more than one next token. DeepInfer uses DFlash as its MTP module. DEEPINFER_USE_NEXTN_DECODE sets the number of drafts (default 5).","a":["nextn","multi-token prediction"]},{"k":"term","t":"NCCL","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-nccl","s":"NVIDIA Collective Communications Library. It moves tensors between NVIDIA GPUs (all-reduce, all-to-all and others). PyTorch calls it the \"nccl\" backend.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"NPU","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-npu","s":"Neural Processing Unit. Huawei's name for its Ascend AI chips. In DeepInfer, an NPU does the same work as a GPU.","a":["Ascend"]},{"k":"term","t":"paged KV cache","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-paged-kv-cache","s":"A KV cache that is split into fixed-size blocks. A sequence gets blocks one at a time, from anywhere in the pool, and a block table records where they are.","a":["paging","paged attention","PagedAttention"]},{"k":"term","t":"pinned memory","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-pinned-memory","s":"CPU memory that the operating system cannot move or swap out. The GPU or NPU can copy from it directly (DMA), so copies are faster.","a":["page-locked memory"]},{"k":"term","t":"Platform object","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-platform","s":"The object in deepinfer/platform.py that holds the hardware choices: kernel folder, communication backend, FP8 scale-factor type, memory pinning.","a":["PLATFORM","platform"]},{"k":"term","t":"preemption","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-preemption","s":"The scheduler takes the KV blocks away from a running sequence because the pool is full. The sequence stops, or waits and is computed again later.","a":["preempt","preempted","recompute"]},{"k":"term","t":"prefill","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-prefill","s":"The first phase of generation. The model reads all prompt tokens in one pass and fills the KV cache for them.","a":["prompt phase","prefill step"]},{"k":"term","t":"process group","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-process-group","s":"A set of ranks that communicate through torch.distributed. Each group uses one backend, for example NCCL, HCCL or Gloo.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"pybind11","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-pybind11","s":"A C++ library that makes C++ functions and classes callable from Python. DeepInfer uses it to build deepinfer._C.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"query, key, value","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-query-key-value","s":"Three vectors that attention makes for each token. The query asks, the keys of earlier tokens answer, and the values carry the content that is mixed.","a":["Q K V","qkv","key","value","query"]},{"k":"term","t":"rank","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-rank","s":"The number of one process in a distributed job. In DeepInfer, one rank normally drives one GPU or NPU.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"RequestOutputPool","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-request-output-pool","s":"A C++ pool of RequestOutput objects. step() returns uint64 handles into this pool. The engine gives the objects back to the pool one step later.","a":["RequestOutput","request output"]},{"k":"term","t":"SamplingParams","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-sampling-params","s":"The settings of one request: temperature, top_p, top_k, max_tokens, seed and more. The engine copies them into the C++ sequence once.","a":["sampling parameters","temperature","max_tokens"]},{"k":"term","t":"scale factor","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-scale-factor","s":"A number that multiplies a block of low-precision values to give their real size. DeepInfer packs one-byte UE8M0 scale factors into int32 (NVIDIA, 4 per value) or int16 (Ascend, 2 per value).","a":["sf"]},{"k":"term","t":"scheduler","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-scheduler","s":"The C++ object that decides, in each engine step, which sequences run, how many tokens each one sends, and which KV blocks each one gets.","a":["Scheduler","schedule"]},{"k":"term","t":"sequence","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-sequence","s":"The engine object for one request: its tokens, its state (waiting, running, finished) and its KV cache blocks.","a":["seq","Sequence"]},{"k":"term","t":"sliding-window attention","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-sliding-window-attention","s":"Attention that looks only at the most recent W tokens (the window), not at all earlier tokens. Its cache has a fixed size per sequence.","a":["SWA","swa","local attention"]},{"k":"term","t":"SM","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-sm","s":"Streaming Multiprocessor: one compute unit inside an NVIDIA GPU. \"SM100\" names the NVIDIA Blackwell data-center GPUs. DeepInfer checks only that the compute capability is 10.x.","a":["SM100","streaming multiprocessor"]},{"k":"term","t":"speculative decoding","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-speculative-decoding","s":"A small module guesses the next tokens (drafts). The main model checks all drafts in one step and keeps the correct prefix, so one step can make several tokens.","a":["speculation","verification"]},{"k":"term","t":"state slot","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-state-slot","s":"A fixed-size area of device memory per running sequence in DeepInfer. It holds the sliding-window cache and the compression state of that sequence.","a":["state_id","StateBlock","state cache"]},{"k":"term","t":"structured output","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-structured-output","s":"Output that must follow a grammar, for example a JSON schema. A matcher masks every token that the grammar does not allow.","a":["SO","so_args","xgrammar"]},{"k":"term","t":"tensor","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-tensor","s":"A multi-dimensional array of numbers, for example a vector or a matrix. A PyTorch tensor is in CPU memory or in GPU/NPU memory.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"TileLang","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-tilelang","s":"A Python language for writing GPU and NPU kernels. DeepInfer keeps one folder of TileLang kernels for CUDA and one for Ascend.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"token","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-token","s":"The unit of text that a model reads and writes: a word, a part of a word, or a symbol. The model sees each token as an integer id.","a":["tokens","token id"]},{"k":"term","t":"tokenizer","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-tokenizer","s":"The program that cuts text into tokens and gives each token an integer id. It also turns ids back into text (decode).","a":["tokenize","detokenize"]},{"k":"term","t":"torch_npu","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-torch-npu","s":"Huawei's PyTorch plug-in for Ascend NPUs. It adds the torch.npu module and the HCCL backend to PyTorch.","a":[]},{"k":"term","t":"vendor library","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-vendor-library","s":"An external kernel library in vendor/ (FlashMLA, DeepGEMM, DeepEP, DeepSelect). It is a git submodule. This site explains only how DeepInfer calls it.","a":["vendor/"]},{"k":"term","t":"visible devices","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-visible-devices","s":"The devices a process can use, set by CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES (NVIDIA) or ASCEND_RT_VISIBLE_DEVICES (Ascend). Device 0 is the first visible one.","a":["CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES","ASCEND_RT_VISIBLE_DEVICES"]},{"k":"term","t":"ZOS","u":"reference/glossary.html#term-zos","s":"Zero-overhead scheduling. The CPU prepares and post-processes one step while the device runs the next, so the CPU work does not stop the device.","a":["zero-overhead scheduling","DEEPINFER_ZERO_OVERHEAD_SCHEDULING"]}];
